/-!
# The relative morphism functor is an algebraic space (Stacks 0D1C)

Let `z : Z ⟶ Q` and `x : X ⟶ Q` be morphisms of algebraic spaces over a scheme `S` of a big fppf
site, with `x` of finite presentation and separated and `z` of finite presentation, flat and
proper. Stacks 0D1C asserts that `Mor_Q(Z, X)` is an algebraic space locally of finite
presentation over `Q`.

The argument is short once its two inputs are available. The graph transformation of Stacks 0D1A
realises `Mor_Q(Z, X)` inside the Hilbert functor of the ambient space `Z ×_Q X` over `Q`, and
Stacks 0D1B says that this is an open immersion; the ambient space is of finite presentation and
separated over `Q`, so Stacks 0D01 makes that Hilbert functor an algebraic space locally of finite
presentation over `Q`; and an open subspace of an algebraic space is an algebraic space, with the
composite to the base still locally of finite presentation.

Stacks 0D01 enters in the form the proof consumes it,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.HasHilbertModelsOver`, which holds over every algebraic space `Q`:
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.hasHilbertModelsOver_of_isAlgebraicSpace`. The Hilbert functor of
`W ⟶ Q` is the Quot functor of `𝒪_W` (Stacks 0D00), whose models are algebraic spaces by
Stacks 09TU because `𝒪_W` is étale-locally generated by finitely many sections, and whose
projection to `Q` is locally of finite presentation because `𝒪_W` is of finite presentation.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.HasHilbertModelsOver`: Stacks 0D01 for the algebraic spaces over `Q`,
  in the form the proof below consumes it.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.morToHilbertModel`: the graph transformation of Stacks 0D1A, valued in
  a small model of the Hilbert presheaf.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.hasHilbertModelsOver_of_isAlgebraicSpace`: Stacks 0D01 over an
  algebraic space `Q`, in the form `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.HasHilbertModelsOver`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFinitePresentation_graphAmbientMap` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isSeparated_graphAmbientMap`: the ambient space `Z ×_Q X` of the graph
  construction is of finite presentation, respectively separated, over `Q`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.morToHilbertModel_comp_toBase`: the realisation of `Mor_Q(Z, X)` in the
  model lies over the projection of `Mor_Q(Z, X)` to `Q`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isAlgebraicSpace_relativeHom`: **Stacks 0D1C**, algebraicity.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_relativeHomProjection`: **Stacks 0D1C**,
  local finite presentation over the base.

## Implementation notes

The finite presentation and separatedness of `Z ×_Q X ⟶ Q` are read off its factorisation
`pr_Z` followed by `z`, rather than off `pr_X` followed by `x`: the structure morphism
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.graphAmbientMap` is literally that composite, so no rewriting along
`CategoryTheory.Limits.pullback.condition` is needed. The two factors need exactly the finite
presentation of `x` and `z`, respectively their separatedness, so the hypotheses are the same
either way.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0D1C](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D1C)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0D1A](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D1A)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0D1B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D1B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0D01](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D01)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

universe u

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S}
    {Z X Q : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} (z : Z ⟶ Q) (x : X ⟶ Q)
    (hZ : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS Z) (hX : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS X)
    (hQ : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS Q)

/-- **Stacks 0D01** for the algebraic spaces over `Q`, in the form the proof of Stacks 0D1C
consumes it: every morphism to `Q` of finite presentation and separated admits a small model of
its Hilbert presheaf which is an algebraic space over `S` and whose projection to `Q` is locally
of finite presentation. -/
def HasHilbertModelsOver : Prop :=
  ∀ (W : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (f : W ⟶ (⟨Q, hQ⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)),
    IsFinitePresentation B S hS f.hom → IsSeparated B S hS f.hom →
      ∃ M : HilbertPresheafModel f, IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS M.presheaf ∧
        IsLocallyOfFinitePresentation B S hS M.toBase

/-- **Stacks 0D01 over an algebraic space `Q`.** Every morphism `W ⟶ Q` of finite presentation
and separated has a model of its Hilbert presheaf which is an algebraic space over `S`, with
projection to `Q` locally of finite presentation.

A model `N` of the Quot presheaf of `𝒪_W` exists, and it is an algebraic space by Stacks 09TU,
`𝒪_W` being étale-locally generated by finitely many sections; its projection to `Q` is locally
of finite presentation because `𝒪_W` is of finite presentation; and `Hilb_{W/Q} = Quot_{𝒪_W/W/Q}`
over `Q` by Stacks 0D00. -/
theorem hasHilbertModelsOver_of_isAlgebraicSpace : HasHilbertModelsOver hQ := by
  intro W f hfp hsep
  obtain ⟨N, -, -⟩ := (structureSheafQuotSituation f hfp).exists_quotSitePresheafModel
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := exists_hilbertPresheafIso_quotSitePresheaf f hfp
  have hN : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS N.presheaf :=
    QuotSituation.isAlgebraicSpace_quotSitePresheafModel_of_isEtaleLocallyGeneratedBelow
      (structureSheafQuotSituation f hfp) hsep
      ⟨Cardinal.aleph0, B.aleph0_lt_cutoff, isEtaleLocallyGeneratedBelow_structureSheafModule W⟩ N
  exact exists_hilbertPresheafModel_isAlgebraicSpace (structureSheafQuotSituation f hfp) f hfp
    hsep N hN
    (N.isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_toBase hN
      (show (structureSheafModule B S hS W).IsFinitePresentationOnSite from
        SheafOfModules.isFinitePresentationOnSite_unit)) e he

/-- The ambient space `Z ×_Q X` of the graph construction is of finite presentation over `Q` when
`z` and `x` are: its structure morphism is the base change of `x` along `z` followed by `z`. -/
theorem isFinitePresentation_graphAmbientMap (hz : IsFinitePresentation B S hS z)
    (hx : IsFinitePresentation B S hS x) :
    IsFinitePresentation B S hS (graphAmbientMap B S hS z x hZ hX hQ).hom := by
  have hfst : IsFinitePresentation B S hS (pullback.fst z x) := by
    have hpb := AlgebraicSpaces.isPullback_fiberProduct B S hS
      (ObjectProperty.homMk z : (⟨Z, hZ⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) ⟶ ⟨Q, hQ⟩)
      (ObjectProperty.homMk x : (⟨X, hX⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) ⟶ ⟨Q, hQ⟩)
    exact (isFinitePresentation_isStableUnderBaseChange B S hS).of_isPullback hpb.flip hx
  exact isFinitePresentation_comp B S hS (graphAmbient B S hS z x hZ hX hQ).property hZ hQ
    (pullback.fst z x) z hfst hz

/-- The ambient space `Z ×_Q X` of the graph construction is separated over `Q` when `z` and `x`
are: its structure morphism is the base change of `x` along `z` followed by `z`. -/
theorem isSeparated_graphAmbientMap (hz : IsSeparated B S hS z) (hx : IsSeparated B S hS x) :
    IsSeparated B S hS (graphAmbientMap B S hS z x hZ hX hQ).hom :=
  isSeparated_comp B S hS (pullback.fst z x) z
    (isSeparated_pullback_fst_of_snd B S hS x z (isSeparated_pullback B S hS x z hx)) hz

/-- The graph transformation of Stacks 0D1A, valued in a small model of the Hilbert presheaf of
the ambient space `Z ×_Q X` over `Q`. -/
def morToHilbertModel (M : HilbertPresheafModel (graphAmbientMap B S hS z x hZ hX hQ))
    (hsep : IsSeparated B S hS x) (hfp : IsFinitePresentation B S hS z)
    (hflat : IsFlat B S hS z) (hproper : IsProper B S hS z) :
    relativeHom B S hS Z X Q z x hZ hX hQ ⟶ M.presheaf :=
  M.mapFrom (graphTransformation hZ hX hQ hsep hfp hflat hproper)

/-- The realisation of `Mor_Q(Z, X)` in a model of the Hilbert presheaf lies over the projection
of `Mor_Q(Z, X)` to `Q`: both read off the first component of a relative morphism. -/
theorem morToHilbertModel_comp_toBase
    (M : HilbertPresheafModel (graphAmbientMap B S hS z x hZ hX hQ))
    (hsep : IsSeparated B S hS x) (hfp : IsFinitePresentation B S hS z)
    (hflat : IsFlat B S hS z) (hproper : IsProper B S hS z) :
    morToHilbertModel z x hZ hX hQ M hsep hfp hflat hproper ≫ M.toBase =
      relativeHomProjection B S hS Z X Q z x hZ hX hQ := by
  ext T s
  cases T
  rename_i T
  refine (M.toBase_mapFrom_app_apply
    (graphTransformation hZ hX hQ hsep hfp hflat hproper) (Opposite.op T) s).trans ?_
  rw [hilbertPresheafToBase_app_apply, graphTransformation_app_toBase]
  exact ((relativeHomData B S hS Z X Q z x hZ hX hQ).projection_sections T s).symm

/-- **Stacks 0D1B** for a model of the Hilbert presheaf: the realisation of `Mor_Q(Z, X)` in the
model is an open immersion. -/
theorem morToHilbertModel_isOpenImmersion
    (M : HilbertPresheafModel (graphAmbientMap B S hS z x hZ hX hQ))
    (hsep : IsSeparated B S hS x) (hfp : IsFinitePresentation B S hS z)
    (hflat : IsFlat B S hS z) (hproper : IsProper B S hS z) :
    IsOpenImmersion B S hS (morToHilbertModel z x hZ hX hQ M hsep hfp hflat hproper) :=
  M.relative_mapFrom _ _
    (graphTransformation_relative_isOpenImmersion z x hZ hX hQ hsep hfp hflat hproper)

/-- The ambient space `Z ×_Q X` of the graph construction has a model of its Hilbert presheaf
which is an algebraic space, with projection to `Q` locally of finite presentation. -/
private theorem exists_hilbertModel_graphAmbientMap (hx_fp : IsFinitePresentation B S hS x)
    (hx_sep : IsSeparated B S hS x) (hz_fp : IsFinitePresentation B S hS z)
    (hz_proper : IsProper B S hS z) :
    ∃ M : HilbertPresheafModel (graphAmbientMap B S hS z x hZ hX hQ),
      IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS M.presheaf ∧ IsLocallyOfFinitePresentation B S hS M.toBase :=
  hasHilbertModelsOver_of_isAlgebraicSpace hQ _ (graphAmbientMap B S hS z x hZ hX hQ)
    (isFinitePresentation_graphAmbientMap z x hZ hX hQ hz_fp hx_fp)
    (isSeparated_graphAmbientMap z x hZ hX hQ hz_proper.1 hx_sep)

/-- **Stacks 0D1C**, algebraicity. For `x` of finite presentation and separated and `z` of finite
presentation, flat and proper, the relative morphism functor `Mor_Q(Z, X)` is an algebraic space
over `S`.

It is realised as an open subspace of a model of the Hilbert functor of `Z ×_Q X` over `Q` by
Stacks 0D1A and 0D1B, and that model is an algebraic space by Stacks 0D01,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.hasHilbertModelsOver_of_isAlgebraicSpace`; an open immersion is
representable, so Stacks 02WY transfers algebraicity to the source. -/
@[stacks 0D1C "algebraicity"]
theorem isAlgebraicSpace_relativeHom (hx_fp : IsFinitePresentation B S hS x)
    (hx_sep : IsSeparated B S hS x) (hz_fp : IsFinitePresentation B S hS z)
    (hz_flat : IsFlat B S hS z) (hz_proper : IsProper B S hS z) :
    IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS (relativeHom B S hS Z X Q z x hZ hX hQ) := by
  obtain ⟨M, hM, -⟩ := exists_hilbertModel_graphAmbientMap z x hZ hX hQ hx_fp hx_sep hz_fp hz_proper
  exact isAlgebraicSpace_of_relativelyRepresentable B S hS
    (morToHilbertModel z x hZ hX hQ M hx_sep hz_fp hz_flat hz_proper)
    (morToHilbertModel_isOpenImmersion z x hZ hX hQ M hx_sep hz_fp hz_flat hz_proper).1 hM

/-- **Stacks 0D1C**, local finite presentation over the base. For `x` of finite presentation and
separated and `z` of finite presentation, flat and proper, the projection
`Mor_Q(Z, X) ⟶ Q` is locally of finite presentation.

The projection factors through a model of the Hilbert functor of `Z ×_Q X` over `Q`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.morToHilbertModel_comp_toBase`); the first factor is an open immersion,
hence locally of finite presentation, and the second is locally of finite presentation by
Stacks 0D01, `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.hasHilbertModelsOver_of_isAlgebraicSpace`. -/
@[stacks 0D1C "local finite presentation over the base"]
theorem isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_relativeHomProjection
    (hx_fp : IsFinitePresentation B S hS x) (hx_sep : IsSeparated B S hS x)
    (hz_fp : IsFinitePresentation B S hS z) (hz_flat : IsFlat B S hS z)
    (hz_proper : IsProper B S hS z) :
    IsLocallyOfFinitePresentation B S hS
      (relativeHomProjection B S hS Z X Q z x hZ hX hQ) := by
  obtain ⟨M, hM, hMlfp⟩ :=
    exists_hilbertModel_graphAmbientMap z x hZ hX hQ hx_fp hx_sep hz_fp hz_proper
  have hopen := morToHilbertModel_isOpenImmersion z x hZ hX hQ M hx_sep hz_fp hz_flat hz_proper
  have halg := isAlgebraicSpace_relativeHom z x hZ hX hQ hx_fp hx_sep hz_fp hz_flat hz_proper
  have hcomp := isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_comp B S hS halg hM hQ
    (morToHilbertModel z x hZ hX hQ M hx_sep hz_fp hz_flat hz_proper) M.toBase
    (isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_of_isOpenImmersion B S hS hopen) hMlfp
  exact morToHilbertModel_comp_toBase z x hZ hX hQ M hx_sep hz_fp hz_flat hz_proper ▸ hcomp

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
